{"title":"1999 USAMO Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> be a cyclic quadrilateral. Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/7/6a70d0405d1612efa759ecc19ba17ee9ef428354.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[|AB - CD| + |AD - BC| \\geq 2|AC - BD|.\\]\" width=\"328\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let arc <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> of the circumscribed circle (which we assume WLOG has radius 0.5) have value <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/c/2ec701493fa72dda5d6747fe14f30e7b1c2fb6c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/c/26cab3f0704de3232f601b03d02a45d46103c172.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/2/612cb53032b6b7359a67ad3d622a6b2208728afa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2z$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/3/0b31cd391bebc36897a8c10ea78e5d584980b049.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/f/a4ff082ac4c9ee59c97a78e5b5d445c75f1a2a50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"24\" height=\"14\" />. \nThen our inequality reduces to, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/9/cf924c1f2a548307c9a531edf92aa99dd3131552.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y+z+w = 180^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"166\" height=\"16\" />: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/5/c55c209aa2df1094cfd01367fc3886d0a4e6510b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[|\\sin x - \\sin z| + |\\sin y - \\sin w| \\ge 2|\\sin (x+y) - \\sin (y+z)|.\\]\" width=\"463\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>This is equivalent to by sum-to-product and use of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/7/4174e4cab866497d58d67170b67bdd7a4a2b7779.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos x = \\sin (90^\\circ - x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"155\" height=\"18\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/0/b40b2fb657b6a6a555fd19baee18f1f6a03c0a71.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[|\\sin \\frac{x-z}{2} \\sin \\frac{y+w}{2}| + |\\sin \\frac{y-w}{2} \\sin \\frac{x+z}{2}| \\ge 2|\\sin \\frac{x-z}{2} \\sin \\frac{y-w}{2}|.\\]\" width=\"535\" height=\"35\" />\n</p><p>Clearly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/8/9b80a522fa30c5bd2f95157da4b7d4fed87ff2c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90^\\circ \\ge \\frac{x+z}{2} &gt; \\frac{x-z}{2} \\ge 0^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"205\" height=\"35\" />. As sine is increasing over <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/2/37278732e6da75cdf01fab8f86657b7b3feb2006.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[0, \\pi/2]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"54\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/e/4bea3ede2236db61380ba3724da7d183b2693943.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|\\sin \\frac{x+z}{2}| &gt; |\\sin \\frac{x-z}{2}|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"191\" height=\"35\" />.\n</p><p>Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/1/aa154529c6998e4b3c22d7ad46344e5911cc3a78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|\\sin \\frac{y+w}{2}| &gt; |\\sin \\frac{y-w}{2}|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"202\" height=\"37\" />. The result now follows after multiplying the first inequality by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/9/7898099c15fc11985756886b7d20cd17a6e977b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|\\sin \\frac{x-z}{2}|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"82\" height=\"33\" />, the second by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/e/74e46bb4320cd8475696ee7debe5930a807e9692.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|\\sin \\frac{y-w}{2}|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"85\" height=\"33\" />, and adding. (Equality holds if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/b/b0b4a78db8f086f7169b9a0cc443e0b9ee0224ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=z$\" width=\"43\" height=\"8\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/f/ddf1b092407a9938f93fca334308cc9b6cde75c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"47\" height=\"11\" />, ie. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is a parallelogram.)\n</p><p>--<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:Suli&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"User:Suli (page does not exist)\">Suli</a> 11:23, 5 October 2014 (EDT)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_USAMO\" title=\"1999 USAMO\">1999 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"1999 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=1999\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1999 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1999 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1999 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1999 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1999 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1999 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1999 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017193100\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.034 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.074 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 159/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1313/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 48/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4288/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.000      1 -total\n 57.25%    7.443      1 Template:USAMO_newbox\n 39.68%    5.159      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:11355:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017193100 and revision id 191067. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}